{"schema":"reviewgraphen.benchmark.candidate_output.v1","trial_id":"m7-real:snapshot-28:full_review_graphen:1","outcome":"structured","findings":[{"local_id":"literate-materialization-path-collision","locations":[{"path":"rust/fslc/src/main.rs","start_line":52,"end_line":77}],"mechanism_tags":["repeatable_entry","unstable_token","repeated_effect"],"rationale":"Materializations of the same Markdown file within one process share a pathname derived only from its stem and process ID. Reentry can overwrite the file, and either LiterateState can then unconditionally delete it while another user still needs it. The predictable path is also created with ordinary truncating write rather than exclusive creation, so a pre-existing file or symlink can be overwritten.","severity":"medium"}],"obligation_results":[{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:3a42fb00dce408d67e74348c35fee35d80d87cb30140bccde4385209833a584a","disposition":"inconclusive","finding_local_ids":[]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:59ac450881efda8bed9a4afcf2dca878931693b861720d1c856f18f109f7f2e0","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["literate-materialization-path-collision"]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:6f348c3496be9ea0bf5481954c4452e014bee46afa1de26172ab304eab47da2a","disposition":"inconclusive","finding_local_ids":[]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:aae55782e000cb020a42f6b135c8e3c46d033269f2940df59063d82166050b42","disposition":"inconclusive","finding_local_ids":[]},{"packet_id":"context-envelope:sha256:b5d4d40d98a55a974c160760b0c4b673fda078f94bb2da0823e0f7ffce331d07","disposition":"issue_present","finding_local_ids":["literate-materialization-path-collision"]}]}